===================================================================
Build artifacts
===================================================================
These are directories and files created by your Makefile.
Ignoring the entire directories is the cleanest approach.

bin/
lib/
Also ignore common object and executable file extensions,
just in case they are created elsewhere.

*.o
*.exe
*.out
*.elf
===================================================================
Libraries
===================================================================
Your Makefile generates static (.a) and shared (.so) libraries
in the 'lib/' directory, which is already ignored above.
These lines are for extra safety.

*.a
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
# ===================================================================
# Documentation
# ===================================================================
# Ignore the directory where Doxygen generates the HTML output.
# We chose 'html/' as the modern standard. I've also included
# the old path from your Makefile's clean rule.

html/
latex/
man/
docs/doxygen_output/
!docs/html/
===================================================================
IDE / Editor Configuration Files
===================================================================
Ignore settings and workspace files from common editors.

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.cproject
.project
===================================================================
Miscellaneous
===================================================================
Ignore crash dump files (common on Linux)

core
Ignore log files

*.log
